1074, 0.006716649979352951, 0.04572121426463127, -0.08026371151208878, -0.017796581611037254, -0.05175035819411278, 0.03143724054098129, 0.03364915773272514, 0.015670178458094597, -0.023771440610289574, 0.02178487926721573, -0.0508037805557251, -9.494723053649068e-05, 0.06983762979507446, -0.026679594069719315, -0.01702256128191948, -1.3230130768704385e-08, 0.011090610176324844, 0.01118417363613844, -0.009632030501961708, 0.04433747008442879, -0.034646403044462204, -0.016458986327052116, -0.032158445566892624, -0.035323366522789, 0.01608031429350376, -0.023991089314222336, -0.004789501428604126, 0.0014435580233111978, 0.075881727039814, 0.06153957173228264, 0.0015562546905130148, -0.048710133880376816, -0.04688240960240364, 0.0722460225224495, -0.07678873836994171, -0.022217197343707085, -0.015323413535952568, 0.08082066476345062, 0.0068257395178079605, 0.02143697254359722, -0.007112422492355108, 0.04183943197131157, -0.03778025507926941, 0.0009092007530853152, 0.058128904551267624, 0.03408985584974289, -0.07070945203304291, -0.10757222771644592, -0.03394373878836632, -0.10945061594247818, 0.004776631481945515, -0.0949372947216034, 0.004259540233761072, -0.0232214517891407, 0.06709448993206024, -0.07902196049690247, 0.0034966059029102325, 0.041402049362659454, 0.0246844831854105, 0.08181523531675339, -0.03587554395198822, -0.0871448665857315, 0.014732623472809792, 0.03402633219957352, -0.005123750306665897, 0.010708301328122616, 0.005247962661087513, -0.01099270861595869, -0.06178484484553337, -0.012767858803272247, -0.02108844742178917, -0.06596056371927261, -0.010036718100309372, 0.042304426431655884, -0.05649419501423836, -0.024842163547873497, -0.0026820318307727575, 0.05415749177336693, 0.00913761556148529, 0.012234422378242016], \"response_payload\": {\"response\": \"Certainly! To fix responsive CSS issues, you can follow these steps:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Check Your CSS File**: Ensure that your CSS file is correctly structured and contains the necessary media queries for responsiveness. A basic structure might look like this:\\\\n\\\\n    ```css\\\\n    /* Basic media query for screens smaller than 768px */\\\\n    @media (max-width: 768px) {\\\\n        /* Styles for screens smaller than 768px */\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    /* Basic media query for screens larger than 768px */\\\\n    @media (min-width: 769px) {\\\\n        /* Styles for screens larger than 768px */\\\\n    }\\\\n    ```\\\\n\\\\n2. **Use Proper Units**: Make sure you\\'re using the appropriate units for your media queries, such as `em`, `rem`, `vw`, or `vh`. For example:\\\\n\\\\n    ```css\\\\n    @media (min-width: 768px) {\\\\n        .your-class {\\\\n            font-size: 1.2rem;\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n    ```\\\\n\\\\n3. **Test Responsiveness**: Use browser developer tools (usually accessible by pressing `F12` or right-clicking and selecting \\\\\"Inspect\\\\\") to test the responsiveness of your website. Check the media queries in the \\\\\"Styles\\\\\" tab to ensure they are being applied correctly.\\\\n\\\\n4. **Use Flexbox or Grid**: If you\\'re using a grid or flexbox layout, ensure that your media queries are correctly applied to the grid or flex container. For example:\\\\n\\\\n    ```css\\\\n    .your-container {\\\\n        display: flex;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    @media (min-width: 768px) {\\\\n        .your-container {\\\\n            flex-direction: row;\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    @media (max-width: 767px) {\\\\n        .your-container {\\\\n            flex-direction: column;\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n    ```\\\\n\\\\n5. **Check for Conflicting Styles**: Sometimes, other CSS rules may conflict with your media queries. Make sure that your media queries are not being overridden by other styles.\\\\n\\\\n6. **Use Responsiveness Plugins**: If you\\'re using a content management system (CMS) like WordPress, consider using plugins like \\\\\"Responsive Images\\\\\" or \\\\\"Responsive CSS\\\\\" to ensure that your images and layouts are responsive.\\\\n\\\\n7. **Review Your HTML Structure**: Ensure that your HTML structure is consistent with your media queries. For example, if you\\'re using a responsive grid, make sure that your HTML structure matches the media queries.\\\\n\\\\nBy following these steps, you should be able to identify and fix the responsive CSS issues on your website.\", \"status_message\": \"completed_with_fallback\"}}', 'semantic_cache_fill:d1a3a82a-ea6c-4438-9fc3-e3c6bfc5c854:local:20260328151050_15b85a0b:d3583db0ce410f7322867050af04aa8ed2decf4ccce0f0a581b9bc59e5a5979e', 0, 1, None, None, None, None, '2026-03-28 15:11:50.138829', '2026-03-28 15:11:50.138836', '2026-03-28 15:11:50.138840', None)) completed"}
